; Default-stack ops for the kernel primitives. Generated by
; tools/generate_adapters.py from include/primitives.json: do not edit by hand.

;----- Array

;-> ( T I -- x ) Return the zero-based element at index list `I` of array `T`.
(() FETCH) (->) PUSH
;. ( A B U -- C ) Apply the binary op held by unit `U` to every pair of elements of numbers or arrays `A` and `B`, aligning shapes from the right. The op runs with the pair on top and must leave exactly one number.
(() BROADCAST) (.) PUSH
;.. ( T axis-or-() U -- x-or-T' ) Fold array `T` over all axes or along one zero-based axis with the binary op held by unit `U`, from left to right starting at each slice's first element. Each step runs `U` with the accumulator and the next element on top; it must leave exactly one number. An empty slice raises `Domain-Error`.
(() REDUCE) (..) PUSH
;<- ( T I x -- T' ) Return `T` with `x` at zero-based index `I`; `T` remains unchanged.
(() STORE) (<-) PUSH
;array ( F Q -- T ) Validate flat numeric data `F` and shape `Q` and construct array `T`.
(() ARRAY) (array) PUSH
;chunk ( T n -- C ) Split rank-one array `T` into `n` ordered rank-one array chunks.
(() CHUNK) (chunk) PUSH
;concat ( C -- T ) Concatenate an ordered list of rank-one array chunks.
(() CONCAT) (concat) PUSH
;dot ( A B -- x ) Return the dot product of rank-one arrays `A` and `B`.
(() DOT) (dot) PUSH
;matmul ( A B -- T ) Multiply rank-two arrays `A` and `B`.
(() MATMUL) (matmul) PUSH
;mean ( T axis-or-() -- x-or-T' ) Compute the arithmetic mean globally or along one axis.
(() MEAN) (mean) PUSH
;median ( T axis-or-() -- x-or-T' ) Compute the median globally or along one axis.
(() MEDIAN) (median) PUSH
;outer ( A B -- T ) Return the rank-two outer product of rank-one arrays `A` and `B`.
(() OUTER) (outer) PUSH
;rank ( T -- n ) Return the rank of array `T`.
(() RANK) (rank) PUSH
;reshape ( T Q -- T' ) Return `T` with shape `Q`; the element count must not change.
(() RESHAPE) (reshape) PUSH
;shape ( T -- Q ) Return the shape list of array `T`.
(() SHAPE) (shape) PUSH
;transpose ( T -- T' ) Transpose rank-two array `T`.
(() TRANSPOSE) (transpose) PUSH

;----- Control

;abort ( -- ) Abandon the current top-level run.
(() ABORT) (abort) PUSH
;apply ( L -- ... ) Execute the elements of list `L` in order.
(() APPLY) (apply) PUSH
;call ( SETUP BODY CATCHER CLEANUP -- ... ) Run `SETUP` and `BODY`, then `CLEANUP`; after a body error, run `CATCHER` after cleanup.
(() CALL) (call) PUSH
;exit ( C -- ) Terminate with integer exit status `C` from 0 through 255.
(() EXIT) (exit) PUSH
;ifte ( I T E -- ... ) Execute `I`, then execute `T` if its result is positive or `E` otherwise.
(() IFTE) (ifte) PUSH
;lambda ( P -- ) Run the program `P`; inside it, `rec` runs `P` again (anonymous recursion).
(() LAMBDA) (lambda) PUSH
;loop ( C B -- ) Repeat: execute `C`, and if its result is positive execute `B` and start again.
(() LOOP) (loop) PUSH
;parallel ( L Q -- R ) Run quotation `Q` for each item of `L` in isolated workers and collect their final stacks in input order.
(() PARALLEL) (parallel) PUSH
;rec ( -- ) Run again the program of the innermost running `lambda`.
(() REC) (rec) PUSH

;----- Debug

;@ ( -- ) Pause the program here and return to the prompt, which then runs at this point until `STEP`, `NEXT`, `CONTINUE` or `STOP`. It does nothing where the program cannot be paused: in a script or an included file, in a nested run such as `PARALLEL`, and in hosts without a prompt.
(() BREAKPOINT) (@) PUSH
;backtrace ( -- L ) Push the list `L` of the programs being run, innermost first. Each is a list `(NAME PROGRAM INDEX)`: `NAME` is a unit with the op whose call started it (`()` if none did), `PROGRAM` is the list it runs and `INDEX` the number of its elements that have already run.
(() BACKTRACE) (backtrace) PUSH
;continue ( -- ) Resume the paused program until the next `BREAKPOINT` or its end. Raises `Debug-Error` if no program is paused.
(() CONTINUE) (continue) PUSH
;next ( -- ) Resume the paused program and pause again before the next op at the same depth or shallower, running the definitions it calls without pausing. Raises `Debug-Error` if no program is paused.
(() NEXT) (next) PUSH
;step ( -- ) Resume the paused program and pause again before the next op it calls, also inside the definitions it calls. Raises `Debug-Error` if no program is paused.
(() STEP) (step) PUSH
;stop ( -- ) Drop the paused program without running the rest of it, keeping the stacks. Raises `Debug-Error` if no program is paused.
(() STOP) (stop) PUSH

;----- Error

;catch ( T H -- ... ) Run `T` and, on error, run `H` with the error on top; without an error `H` is not run. `H` sees the stack as `T` left it when it failed; the library op `try` restores it first.
(() CATCH) (catch) PUSH
;rethrow ( E -- ) Propagate existing error `E` without recording it again.
(() RETHROW) (rethrow) PUSH
;throw ( L K -- ) Raise an error whose kind is the selector `K` (such as `(Type-Error)`) with data list `L`; any other `K` raises `Type-Error`.
(() THROW) (throw) PUSH

;----- List

;consl ( L U -- L' ) Prepend the element of unit `U` to list `L`.
(() CONSL) (consl) PUSH
;consr ( L U -- L' ) Append the element of unit `U` to list `L`.
(() CONSR) (consr) PUSH
;unconsl ( L -- L' U ) Remove the first element of a non-empty list into a unit.
(() UNCONSL) (unconsl) PUSH
;unconsr ( L -- L' U ) Remove the last element of a non-empty list into a unit.
(() UNCONSR) (unconsr) PUSH
;unit ( X -- U ) Wrap the top value in a one-element list.
(() UNIT) (unit) PUSH

;----- Math

;* ( A B -- C ) Multiply `A` and `B`.
(() MUL) (*) PUSH
;+ ( A B -- C ) Add `A` and `B`.
(() ADD) (+) PUSH
;- ( A B -- C ) Subtract `B` from `A`.
(() SUB) (-) PUSH
;/ ( A B -- C ) Divide `A` by `B` using true division.
(() DIV) (/) PUSH
;// ( A B -- C ) Floor-divide `A` by `B`.
(() IDIV) (//) PUSH
;: ( a b -- L ) The inclusive list from `a` to `b` in steps of 1, like `a 1 b ::`.
(1 1 () ROLL () RANGE) (:) PUSH
;:: ( START STEP END -- L ) Generate an inclusive numeric range from `START` to `END` using `STEP`.
(() RANGE) (::) PUSH
;^ ( A B -- C ) Raise `A` to the power `B`.
(() POW) (^) PUSH
;ratio ( X -- N DEN ) Return the exact numerator and denominator of number `X`.
(() RATIO) (ratio) PUSH

;----- Source

;eval ( T -- ... ) Read the source code in string `T` and run it; a source error raises `Syntax-Error` before anything runs.
(parse apply) (eval) PUSH
;include ( P -- ) Lower and execute the source file named by `P`, even if it was already loaded, after taking out what its earlier load left (its private ops, the items it pushed, its locks and the stacks it made; see the language guide). The default-stack op `require` skips files that were loaded.
(() INCLUDE) (include) PUSH
;included ( P -- 1|0 ) Report whether source file `P` has already been loaded; 0 if its load ended in an error.
(() INCLUDED) (included) PUSH
;parse ( T -- P ) Read the source code in string `T` and leave the program it denotes as the list `P`, without running it. Invalid source raises `Syntax-Error` with the message and the line within `T`.
(() PARSE) (parse) PUSH
;require ( P -- ) Load source file `P` unless it was already loaded; `include` loads it again. A file whose load ended in an error does not count as loaded.
((0 pick included) (drop) (() INCLUDE) ifte) (require) PUSH

;----- Stack

;clear ( -- ) Remove all values.
(() CLEAR) (clear) PUSH
;depth ( -- n ) Return the number of values.
(() DEPTH) (depth) PUSH
;drop ( A -- ) Remove the top value.
(() DROP) (drop) PUSH
;lexicon ( -- L ) Push the list `L` of the selectors of every op that has a stack, that is, every one for which `EXISTS` reports 1, primitives and emptied stacks included, ordered by name. Each selector is a unit containing the op, so it can be used as it is. Filter the list in Bo and map `CLEAR` or `DELETE` over what is left.
(() LEXICON) (lexicon) PUSH
;lock ( -- ) Protect against mutation: it then refuses `PUSH`, `POP`, `CLEAR`, `DELETE` and the like. Locking a locked stack changes nothing. The default stack cannot be locked (`Permission-Error`).
(() LOCK) (lock) PUSH
;pick ( .. An .. A0 n -- .. An .. A0 An ) Copy the zero-based nth value to the top.
(() PICK) (pick) PUSH
;roll ( .. An .. A0 n -- .. A0 An ) Move the zero-based nth value to the top.
(() ROLL) (roll) PUSH
;snapshot ( -- L ) Copy the contents as a list.
(() SNAPSHOT) (snapshot) PUSH
;unlock ( -- ) Remove mutation protection. Unlocking a stack that is not locked, such as the default stack, changes nothing. Unlocking a primitive's stack lets a definition shadow the primitive.
(() UNLOCK) (unlock) PUSH

;----- Stream

;close ( H -- ) Close stream `H`.
(() CLOSE) (close) PUSH
;open ( P M -- H ) Open file `P` with mode `M` and return its handle `H`.
(() OPEN) (open) PUSH
;read ( H -- c ) Read the next character code from stream `H`, or return -1 at end of file.
(() READ) (read) PUSH
;write ( c H -- ) Write character code `c` to stream `H`.
(() WRITE) (write) PUSH

;----- Value

;= ( A B -- 1|0 ) Compare values structurally.
(() EQUAL) (=) PUSH
;name ( K -- N ) Convert the selector `K` to the name `N` of its op, a string; the default-stack selector `()` gives the empty string `()`.
(() NAME) (name) PUSH
;selector ( N -- K ) Convert the string `N`, a valid op name, to the selector `K` of that op; the empty string `()` gives the default-stack selector `()`.
(() SELECTOR) (selector) PUSH
;type ( X -- K ) Return 0 for a number, 1 for a list, or 2 for an op.
(() TYPE) (type) PUSH
;unittype ( U -- K ) Inspect the element type of unit `U`: 0 number, 1 list, or 2 op.
(() UNITTYPE) (unittype) PUSH
